   "report": "Brannoc banked his forge at dusk yesterday and went down the Low Ford road alone, with a lantern and a blanket, between his irons. At the ford one blue light went out. He came back up the road at sunrise with the blanket in his arms, and Chid walked out past the guards to meet him, and walked beside him up the street. They are burying her this morning, behind the shrine, next to the old captain. Nobody has been asked to come."
